# Phase 6 managed composition: census, coexistence and optimization

## Result boundary

The bounded reconciliation/optimization task is complete. ED11 total and the complete future issuer/CNG/X509 composition remain PARTIAL/UNKNOWN. No operational reservation, admission, certificate, CURRENT publication or native qualification is created by this census. The unchanged cap is 2,097,152 bytes. Source and census operations were officially reviewed before application; accepted contracts are unchanged.

The owner-supplied prior ceiling 2,093,415 is reproduced exactly as the conservative SELECTED-size variant: 1,974,299 prepared-root budget +85,576 initial-source caller +18,784 bounded codec pair +128 receipt +4,096 native scratch +10,532 begin local-copy allowance. Current native test measurements distinguish ALL root budget 1,974,283 from SELECTED-size budget 1,974,299. Thus the highest arithmetic bound includes the extra16 bytes even though SELECTED operational applicability remains denied. Earlier ALL labels must not be read as proving that distinction. No legitimate reservation is removed by relabeling it.

After elimination of one redundant local9376byte copy on each affected path, remaining begin allowance is1104byte CONFIG_VIEW +52byte identity=1156. Same formula gives ALL2,084,023 and conservative maximum2,084,039; delta-9376; remaining13,113. Different functions are alternatives, so do not sum the eliminated copy three times. No parser/codec capacity, root array or retained generation shrinks.

## Physical containers versus reservations

See composition-matrix.csv and ed11-census.json. Size-only tests compile with the canonical root/profile and normal SDK in both configurations; their sizeof results match exactly. No root/resource is instantiated by the census executable.

Fixed design graph1,384,376 already includes launcher182,768, C2 owner274,040, participant528,944, two C3 bridges264,896, site manager/connections280, stage pool131,712 and stage leases/borrows1216, plus remaining embedded adapter/padding520. These children are NOT added again. Generic arrays319,488, Secure arrays25,088, scheduler4432, bind144, one existing worker stack65,536 and checkpoint owner scratch8192 produce known reserved layout1,807,256. This is a conservative compiled graph/reservation, not observed process RAM. Some contained pools are dormant/candidate reservations, not enabled functional authorities.

Launcher includes commit105,712 and preparation9952. Commit includes pending packet51,096, committed16,896, slots3456, tickets1024, issuer staging8192 and three issuer snapshots24,576. Pending arrays consume50,688 of that packet; handles/fields/padding are already included. Component-test owner105,736/packet51,120 add24 test-hook bytes and must not replace actual production sizes. Preparation includes source416, participants6408 (including immutable interface copy5928), policy1120 and other fields; do not charge these children twice. Site TLS catalog/profile copies in configuration views, bridges and stages are included by sizeof; native PST/runtime/trust/child allocations remain additional UNKNOWN.

The source preparation formula preserves the existing additional131,072 caller reservation, source material credit32,768 and observed runtime credit3203. The131,072 is an unitemized caller allowance, not proof of one allocated buffer or a spare pool. It is not reassigned to signer/AST or removed by assuming overlapping use. Product activation still needs exact caller composition. The source caller85,576 separately includes AST59,880, source8192, initial resolution1088, diagnostic24, pointer8 and existing stack allowance16,384. Update output1072 is an alternative to initial1088. Existing no-carrier fields9376 and encoded9408 remain separately owned and charged; the patch removes only the ADDITIONAL inner decode copy.

## Function-level lifetime proof

1. pc_root8_validate_no_issuer is a read-only extraction of the original bounded decoder's length/carrier/hash/shape checks. It returns no view, no pointer, authority, pin or resource. pc_root8_decode_no_issuer preserves its own disjointness checks, output clearing, copy and completion semantics, calling the same validator. General ROOT8/LST1 layouts/capacity and historical readers remain unchanged. Callbacks retain their existing synchronous/non-reentrant/immutable-input contract; no validation check is skipped.
2. papacc_configuration_d3_begin08 reads validated bytes from o->committed under the existing owner-thread and critical-section boundary, after confirming no pending/retained writer. Pin/current checks remain. A pin alone is NOT claimed to protect mutable committed bytes: owner serialization, lock and absence of a root-writing worker protect this call. The worker has no root pointer. Existing snapshot/pin/issuer/CAS guards are unchanged. A new packet is exposed only after validation/freeze.
3. papacc_configuration_d3_committed08 reads p->next only after the existing successful native commit, thread signal/close and no active/file/transaction/close-error guards. The packet remains fully retained, not reused or overwritten. Exported output/receipt/used spans remain disjoint from root and each other. Read-only validation and copy remain synchronous; no pointer escapes.
4. papacc_configuration_bootstrap_commit_begin reads the immutable caller image after existing disjointness, identity, custody, authority and Stop checks. The caller must preserve it through this synchronous call, as before; it is frozen into p->next before worker start. No caller or packet lifetime is shortened. Namespace proof/previous scratch and future observed readback buffer are not shared or overwritten by this optimization.
5. Reservation checks remove only the eliminated9376-byte object. D3 begin still prices view+identity via sizeof. Bootstrap uses the same typed conservative residual. Committed export still prices its digest32; source/native/worker stack allowances remain. Compiled Debug rsp allocations: begin1392, committed192, bootstrap368; Release1280,120,520 respectively. These are NOT full call-chain bounds: saved registers, callers, provider and runtime stack remain separate qualification items. Existing16KiB source allowance is preserved, not silently reduced to a single frame.

## Coexistence rules

- Three root slots, issuer images, pins, old Sessions and retained worker arrays remain simultaneously charged. No credit is returned by validation/export, Stop, timeout or remote FINAL.
- AST/source caller, bounded codec pair, frozen packet, old committed history and source material may coexist; the conservative peak retains all these charges. A caller must not reclaim retained bytes to fit a new operation.
- The three validation entry points are separate serialized calls; one existing pending worker/packet cannot service two simultaneous commits. Active/unknown/retained guards are preserved. A second independent caller/output pair still requires separate credit and can be denied.
- CLI config dispatch occurs before normal launch in main.c.api3.inc and returns immediately for config commands. Its transient workspace is68112bytes (derived from actual PC_DOCUMENT/input8193/diagnostic/target alignment). This proves only absence of live runtime dynamic allocations on that entry path, not absence of linked static root objects. Keep fixed static graph charged. Do not generalize this exclusivity to a future in-process live administration command.
- Existing dormant preparation rejects active listener/io/C2/PST graphs. This is not permission to omit their retained/static reservations. Future live signer/config concurrency has no established exclusion and must be priced together unless a factual owner boundary proves otherwise.
- External observer is an existing separate process: explicit hash scratch66,560 and record8192, three handles plus native/CRT/stack overhead; total peak remains UNKNOWN. Python offline join has input bound8MiB plus rows/parser/library overhead. Do not charge them twice to the product2MiB owner or treat them as free: each process needs its own census and host coexistence measurement. No fictitious cross-process combined quota is created.

## Issuer/CSR/X509/signing budget

Known additional one-instance objects, if newly attached: CNG owner472 +portable core216 +backend vtable88 +CSR descriptor24 +public-validation scratch4096 =4896. None is currently instantiated by product startup. Adding only those objects to the conservative known peak would give2,088,935, leaving8217 BEFORE new CSR bytes, TBS/certificate outputs, certificate verification, nested stack, native crypto workspace and retained uncertain work. This number is NOT a ready signer budget.

CSR input maximum/lifetime, complete X509 builder scratch/TBS/DER output, signer and key-generation provider resources, package/transient client-key storage and multiple retained results remain unbounded/not implemented. Existing records/certificate bytes within8192-byte issuer images are not a second registry, but a caller output coexisting with those copies must still be charged. Old CA generation/key work retained during rotation cannot be assumed absent. CNG is not free because its provider is external; same-process managed buffers/handles and provider/kernel/commit must all be priced. A separate issuing process, if ever governed, would still require its own budget and physical coexistence proof; no such architecture is introduced here.

Complete future managed maximum = UNKNOWN, not2,084,039. Known fixed-layout floor/reservation is1,807,256, not a complete minimum process working set. Full process physical/commit/handles/provider/kernel maxima and native retained peaks remain UNKNOWN. Admission, signer activation and authoritative recovery stay DENY. No arbitrary numeric reserve or quota is invented to fill these gaps.

## Validation

Final Debug/Release complete affected candidate/component linkage passes /W4 /WX with zero warnings. Fifteen selected CTests per configuration pass (parser/bridge/LST1/D3/issuer/checkpoint/Windows public validation/CLI/layout/census and interface guards). Native diagnostic scopes: D3 reject/success/conflict/UNKNOWN/Stop and seven ROOT06 codec/pending/history/snapshot cases per configuration pass; bootstrap retained-reference commit seven cases per configuration pass, repeated after the typed guard refinement. Root lifetime nine cases per configuration pass: abort, retained root, snapshot Stop/retention, native-interface consume Stop/retention and catalog live/unknown/Stop.

The first root lifetime invocation omitted the existing test-only enrollment environment and correctly failed before its provider path. That original result is preserved; rerun uses the documented public fixture digest from the existing harness. No fixture is production authority. Real native file/CAS/interface/provider observations are separated from synthetic policy/Session/CA metadata and injected faults. No network, real CA/certificate, native CNG creation/signature or elevated admin proof ran. Existing CNG error-classification and portable issuer fault suites pass; historical native key remains UNKNOWN. Native rollback/retention results do not imply universal crash recovery or DESTROYED after process exit.

## Scoped handoff for signer/X509

Before attaching the existing backend port, specify bounded CSR/TBS/output sizes and ownership from the accepted profile/provider and exact implementation, then measure/compile full call chains and price every concurrently retained result. Reuse existing caller/packet storage only if a future exact proof demonstrates no borrower, active Session, worker or retained dependency; this patch offers no shared pool or blanket reuse. Keep generic131072, source material and snapshots reserved until their own ownership evidence permits a change. Compare the completed graph against the unchanged cap before effects; missing bound or insufficient credit returns DENY.

Preserve serial reservation before sign, uncertain SIGN_REQUESTED retention, exact same-root CURRENT/A/P, no CAS fallback and denied recovery without checkpoint/fencing. The public CSR helper is not a signer or complete X509 builder. Complete those implementations and their memory proof without creating another worker/registry/authority. Administrative positive qualification remains BLOCKED_BY_ENVIRONMENT. This handoff opens no CA, grant, listener or Phase6 release gate.
